repository-code: "https://github.com/Takeyuki-K/k1-mp-ecowalk-public"
abstract: "Simulation study (MuJoCo) on the ROBOTIS AI Sapiens K1 humanoid model with passive spring toe (MP) joints, imitation of human gait data and learned joint relaxation. v5.6.3: walking and running policies switched by a gait manager - walking, running, turning (also on the spot), quick stop, hard braking and re-stance, left/right symmetric. In a same-condition simulation comparison of straight walking against the public ROBOTIS walk_default policy, v5.6.3 has 29 % lower estimated electrical cost of transport (27 % with strict static friction); the walking-only v1.0 had 37 % lower. Not tested on a real robot. Implementation generated with Claude (Anthropic) under the direction of Takeyuki-K."
keywords:
  - humanoid
  - reinforcement learning
  - energy efficiency
  - toe joint
  - variable impedance
  - motion imitation
  - running
  - gait transition
  - MuJoCo
